# 10 - AWS Edge Locations

## 1. Points of Presence (PoPs)
- AWS global locations used to deliver content and services closer to users.
- Include Edge Locations and Regional Edge Caches.

## 2. Edge Locations
- Used by Amazon CloudFront.
- Cache content closer to end users.
- Reduce Latency and improve content delivery speed.

## 3. Regional Edge Caches
- Larger cache locations between Edge Locations and the Origin.
- Help reduce requests to the Origin Server.
- Store content for users across a wider geographical area.

## 4. Amazon CloudFront
- AWS Content Delivery Network (CDN).
- Uses Edge Locations and Regional Edge Caches.
- Delivers cached content with lower Latency.

## 5. Quick Revision

| Concept | Main Purpose |
|---|---|
| PoPs | Global points of presence |
| Edge Locations | Cache content near users |
| Regional Edge Caches | Larger intermediate cache |
| CloudFront | Global content delivery (CDN) |

**Exam Tips:**
- CloudFront → CDN.
- Edge Locations → Low Latency.
- Regional Edge Cache → Larger cache between Edge Location and Origin.
- PoPs → Edge Locations + Regional Edge Caches.